    "evidence_text": "jiant's core dependencies are PyTorch , AllenNLP , and HuggingFace's Transformers .\n\njiant System Overview ::: Task and Model resources in jiant\tjiant supports over 50 tasks.\n\njiant focuses on NLU tasks like MNLI , CommonsenseQA , the Winograd Schema Challenge , and SQuAD .\n\nA full inventory of tasks and task variants is available in the jiant/tasks module.\n\njiant provides support for cutting-edge sentence encoder models, including support for Huggingface's Transformers.\n\nSupported models include: BERT , RoBERTa , XLNet , XLM , GPT , GPT-2 , ALBERT  and ELMo .\n\njiant also supports the from-scratch training of (bidirectional) LSTMs  and deep bag of words models , as well as syntax-aware models such as PRPN  and ON-LSTM .\n\njiant also supports word embeddings such as GloVe .\n\njiant System Overview ::: User Interface\tjiant experiments can be run with a simple CLI: jiant\n\njiant System Overview ::: jiant Development Roadmap\tjiant is actively being developed.\n\njiant code is open source, and jiant invites contributors to open issues or submit pull request to the jiant",
